{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's own claim is that the route was 'far longer than quoted', and the trace confirms a measured excess of 3.22 km over the booked optimal of 9.2 km, which is 35.00% of optimal. That is above the 20% and 0.8 km establishment thresholds, so a deviation is established on this trip's own trace under POL-RD-01. The governing figure is gps_trace.trace_distance_km (12.42 km), not the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km (12.4 km), as POL-RD-01 requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02813", "EV-TRIP-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation is not merely established but MATERIAL: the excess of 3.22 km is 35.00% of optimal, which is below the 50% materiality threshold, and 3.22 km is below the 8.0 km absolute materiality threshold. The materiality gate is therefore NOT crossed, and the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not triggered by materiality. I concede this point: the deviation is established but not material on this trip's own numbers.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02813", "EV-TRIP-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare model on this trip is UPFRONT_QUOTE with a quoted fare of SGD 21.50 and a charged total of SGD 28.30. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, so POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however large the excess. The rider's remedy is limited to the amount by which charged_total exceeds quoted_fare_sgd plus properly chargeable pass-through lines. The fare_breakdown's own derived money block computes that remedy as SGD 6.80, and the payment status is CHARGED with no refund issued.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.pol_rd_11_remedy",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's counterparty statement is 'The meter adds the extra distance.' That is a bare assertion of a metering mechanism, not a traffic advisory, not a rider instruction, and not a point relocation. It cites no evidence ID and invokes no clause. Under POL-RD-08 a general assertion unsupported by an artifact does not discharge the driver's burden, and under POL-RD-13 an uncited traffic excuse carries no weight where no advisory is on file.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-02813-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and the GPS trace's own advisory_area block records an empty advisories list under POL-RD-03. The driver's implicit external-cause excuse therefore cannot be tested against any advisory, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight. The absence itself is citable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02813-01", "EV-GPS-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.advisories",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log for this trip is empty: message_count 0, no messages, no waypoint_hint, no rider instruction of any kind. POL-RD-04 requires a rider instruction recorded in the chat_log with a waypoint_hint the trace can be tested against; with no chat_log content the corroboration test is undecidable on the record, the clause is unavailable, and no distance is excluded from the excess on that ground.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip_record shows no amendment to pickup or dropoff: pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null, original_pickup and original_dropoff are both null, and amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are both null. POL-RD-05 cannot be run and no amended optimal route exists to re-test the deviation against.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null. POL-RD-12's pooled-itinerary baseline does not apply and the booked optimal of 9.2 km is the correct baseline for the POL-RD-01 test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace is clean for policy purposes: 98 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, and no straight-line jump over 500 m. It is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), so no independent corroboration is required and the deviation stands at the measured figure. The admissibility pre-pass also tags it COMPLETE at weight 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's profile does not trigger the POL-RD-08 corroboration uplift: deviation_claims_60d is 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the 4-or-more claims condition is not met and no extra corroboration beyond the gps_trace is required for this claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's profile does not establish a repeat deviation pattern under POL-RD-06: deviation_flags_90d is 0, which is below the 3-or-more threshold, and 0 divided by completed_trips_90d of 260 is 0.00, below the 0.05 ratio threshold. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags of 1 is a near-synonym trap and is NOT the trailing-90-day figure POL-RD-06 asks for; it may not be substituted. No POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral is supported on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare_breakdown carries zero ERP gantries and zero tolls, and the airport surcharge is 0.00 on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport. There is no off-route or phantom gantry line and no wrongly applied surcharge, so no standalone pass-through correction under POL-RD-09 is due. The properly_chargeable total is 0.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.properly_chargeable.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's claim that the route was 'far longer than quoted' is supported by the trace, but the rider's claim that the charge was wrong is not: on an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip the rider is already whole on distance and time, and the only recoverable amount is the SGD 6.80 by which the charged total exceeds the quoted fare plus properly chargeable lines. The rider's contested amount of SGD 7.50 exceeds the recoverable SGD 6.80, and the difference is not recoverable under POL-RD-11.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02813", "EV-GPS-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.charged_over_quote",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

